<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    {%- comment -%}
      The seller's SEO fields from the dashboard: the store's on every page, a product's own
      on its page. An empty one falls back to the product or store name.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign page_title = store.seoTitle | default: store.name -%}
    {%- assign page_description = store.seoDescription | default: store.name -%}
    {%- if product -%}
      {%- assign page_title = product.seo.title | default: product.name -%}
      {%- assign page_description = product.seo.description | default: page_description -%}
    {%- endif %}
    <meta name="description" content="{{ page_description }}">
    <title>{{ page_title }}</title>
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ store.name }}">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ page_title }}">
    <meta property="og:description" content="{{ page_description }}">
    <meta property="og:type" content="{% if product %}product{% else %}website{% endif %}">
    {%- comment -%}
      The card a link unfurls into, in Discord, Slack or X: a product page shows the product's
      first image large, any other page the store's logo as a thumbnail. Both URLs are absolute,
      which link previews require. Previews draw no SVG, so an SVG logo is left out.
      `theme-color` tints Discord's card with the canvas colour (`--color-canvas`).
    {%- endcomment %}
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#101010">
    {%- if product.images.size > 0 %}
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ product.images.first.url }}">
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ product.images.first.altText | default: product.name }}">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    {%- elsif store.logoImageUrl %}
      {%- unless store.logoImageUrl contains '.svg' %}
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ store.logoImageUrl }}">
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="{{ store.name }}">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
      {%- endunless %}
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if product.variants.size > 0 %}
    {%- comment -%}
      The product as schema.org data, which search engines show as a rich result: its name, its
      own description (its SEO one, else its text without Markdown), its images and one Offer
      per variant, priced as a plain decimal in the price's currency. A product with no variant
      has no Offer, which a rich result needs, so it gets none. The page is cached and stock is
      live, so no Offer claims an availability. `json | raw` escapes `<`, so seller text cannot
      close the script element.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign product_description = product.description | markdown | strip_html | strip | default: product.name %}
    {%- if product.seo.description != blank %}
      {%- assign product_description = product.seo.description %}
    {%- endif %}
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "Product",
        "name": {{ product.name | json | raw }},
        "description": {{ product_description | json | raw }},
        {%- if product.images.size > 0 %}
        "image": {{ product.images | map: "url" | json | raw }},
        {%- endif %}
        "offers": [
          {%- for variant in product.variants %}
          {
            "@type": "Offer",
            "name": {{ variant.name | json | raw }},
            "price": {{ variant.unitPrice | money_amount | json | raw }},
            "priceCurrency": {{ variant.unitPrice.currency | json | raw }}
          }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
          {%- endfor %}
        ]
      }
    </script>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- comment -%}
      The `.page-bg` aurora (bg.webp) is the LCP element, but only theme.css references it, so
      the browser would find it after the stylesheet loads. Preload it and Inter with the same
      URLs theme.css uses so each is fetched once.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'bg.webp' | asset_url }}" as="image" type="image/webp" fetchpriority="high">
    <link rel="preload" href="{{ 'inter-latin.woff2' | asset_url }}" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'theme.css' | asset_url }}">
    {{ content_for_head }}
  </head>
  <body class="h-screen overflow-hidden antialiased p-2 bg-canvas">
    <div class="page-bg bg-surface rounded-2xl h-full overflow-y-auto overscroll-none">
      <div class="flex justify-center sticky top-0 z-20">
        <span class="notch inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-5 pb-2 pt-1 text-sm text-white/50">
          Powered by
          <img src="{{ 'novinzo.svg' | asset_url }}" alt="Novinzo" width="16" height="16">
        </span>
      </div>
      <div class="container px-5 lg:px-8 flex flex-col gap-20 lg:gap-40 mx-auto">
        {% section 'header' %}
        <main id="main-content" class="flex flex-col gap-20" role="main">
          {{ content_for_layout }}
        </main>
        {% section 'footer' %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <nz-cart-drawer store-id="{{ store.id }}"></nz-cart-drawer>
    {{ content_for_scripts }}
  </body>
</html>
